Proficiency in graph database concepts and Neo4j specific data modeling. Expertise in extracting entities and relationships from unstructured text to build a knowledge graph. Skill in designing a robust graph schema including nodes, relationships, and properties. Competency in creating and optimizing indexes, including full-text search and vector indexes, for high-performance retrieval. Deep knowledge of the Cypher query language for both data manipulation and complex pattern-matching retrieval. Experience with creating and managing vector embeddings for text chunks and storing them within the graph database. Ability to develop and implement a multi-part, hybrid retrieval strategy combining vector similarity search with structured Cypher queries. Understanding of the Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline and how to effectively use a knowledge graph for context augmentation. Skill in prompt engineering to instruct Large Language Models (LLMs) to use retrieved context exclusively for generation. Strong Python coding skills for building RAG applications, including using libraries like LangChain or LlamaIndex. Practical experience in connecting to Neo4j, executing queries programmatically, and handling query results. Capacity to develop and debug end-to-end proof-of-concept scripts that demonstrate the RAG workflow. Knowledge of performance tuning for Neo4j queries and database configurations. Aptitude for developing data ingestion pipelines to automate the population of a knowledge graph from various data sources. Overall expertise in building a cohesive, end-to-end RAG system leveraging the power of a graph database.